    "reason": "Keep the prior publication-inventory repair contract unchanged and add a cross-surface instruction correction. An explicit feedback request authorizes one sanitized submission, and an existing task's authority covers necessary in-scope bug reports and discussion follow-ups, without a redundant confirmation. Privacy, selected-context, server-authority, no-replay and reporter-completion safeguards are kept. The correction touches canonical feedback and settings skills, every generated client mirror and archive, and the version pins of dependent components. That makes it a deep fix with interaction coverage for version, dependency, package and graph-composition consumers. Prior criteria, modules, fixtures, mapping purposes, pending downstream obligations and the fixed 300-second delivery policy stay unchanged. This selection grants no source publication authority.",
